Translation patch: the OAuth metadata address policy of
crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth/metadata_resolver.rs, so that its pure functions translate (plan
Section 2.3, amendment 2026-11-25: targets N01 and N03-N11; Sections 4, 15, 19 and 23, amendments
2026-11-25; human decisions 2026-11-25: patch 05 with hunks H1-H9 and the module prim, N02
SystemResolver::resolve not a target)

Applies to: the copy of upstream origin/main 7caec762799bece6fba38e4298b8ca7db8bac12c after
01-request-state-wire.patch, 02-phase2-tests.patch, 03-request-state-public.patch and
04-skill-public.patch (scripts/apply-patches.sh applies formal/trusted/patches/*.patch in
file-name order, patch -p1 -F 0, only to the copy in .llbc/work/; the real source is never
patched). Files: crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth/metadata_resolver.rs (blob 03435a2, which
patches 01-04 do not touch) and crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs (blob e434558 after patch 02,
which adds only #[cfg(test)] code there). Generated with git diff from the patch-01..04 copy.
The patch body below is the authoritative content. Toolchain measured: Aeneas
nightly-2026.11.24-fb44cb4, Charon 0.1.324, Rust nightly-2026-09-17.

Not part of this patch (they stay in the repository): the Charon settings in
crates/rmcp/Cargo.toml (eleven start_from entries for N01, N03-N11 and the helpers
with_base_url, allowed_addresses and proxy_host; the opaque entry "url" narrowed to "url::Url";
rmcp::transport::auth::metadata_resolver::Lookup and ::prim added to opaque), the PINNED_DEPS
entry url 2.5.9, TARGETS and PATCH05_TARGETS of scripts/aeneas-translate.sh, the patch05 set of
scripts/check-original-linkage.sh, and the external models of formal/trusted/Rmcp/ (section
"metadata_resolver.rs address policy"). Without this patch N01 AddressClass::of and N08
MetadataAddressResolver::is_allowed translate unmodified (ORIGINAL linkage); N03-N07 and
N09-N11 need it (linkage patch-05).

Stays unverified (not translated, or translated only as an opaque model): N02
SystemResolver::resolve (async OS DNS, not a target); the async shells of
`<MetadataAddressResolver as Resolve>::resolve` (normalize_host, the lookup, `warn!`, the error
message and the Some/None to Ok/Err mapping) and the public with_lookup (one call of
with_base_url); the bodies of prim::system_lookup (opaque value) and prim::proxy_env_values
(the environment read; an opaque constant, as the clock of request_state.rs); the derived Clone
of MetadataAddressResolver and Lookup; URL parsing (url::Url::parse, host, host_str: opaque
functions of the opaque type url::Url, no axiom).

Change (non-test lines only; no test is added or changed). Every hunk replaces code that the
translation cannot handle by calls to the new module `prim`, by a newtype, or by loops and
nested matches, and keeps the computed values:
 prim  New module `prim` at the end of metadata_resolver.rs (before `mod tests`), visible in
       crate::transport::auth, opaque in the translation and modelled in Lean, each the original
       expression: trim_end_dots (`s.trim_end_matches('.')`), ends_with
       (`s.ends_with(suffix)`), contains (`s.contains(pat)`), system_lookup
       (`Lookup(Arc::new(SystemResolver))`), proxy_env_values (the original
       `PROXY_ENV_VARS.iter().filter_map(|var| std::env::var(var).ok())`, collected into a
       Vec). Used by H3, H4, H8 and H9.
 H1  Field `lookup: Arc<dyn Resolve>` becomes `lookup: Lookup`, a new private
     `#[derive(Clone)]` newtype `struct Lookup(Arc<dyn Resolve>)`; resolve calls
     `this.lookup.0.resolve(name)`.
 H2  with_lookup keeps its signature and becomes `Self::with_base_url(base_url, Lookup(lookup))`;
     its body moves to the new private `with_base_url(base_url, lookup: Lookup)`, with the
     guarded arm `Some(Host::Domain(domain)) if ..` written as a nested `match host` with an
     `if`, and `Arc::new([])` written as `Vec::new().into()`.
 H3  new: `Self::with_base_url(base_url, prim::system_lookup())
     .with_proxy_hosts(prim::proxy_env_values())`.
 H4  with_proxy_hosts: the hosts are pushed onto `self.unfiltered_hosts.to_vec()` in a `for`
     loop over `proxies` (instead of `iter().cloned().chain(..).collect()`); the filter_map
     closure moves verbatim to the new private fn `proxy_host`, with `prim::contains` for
     `str::contains`, `"http://".to_owned()` + `push_str` for `format!("http://{proxy}")`, and
     the closure `|host| normalize_host(host)` for the fn item `normalize_host`.
 H5  allowing_private_addresses: `to_vec()`, `push(AddressClass::Private)`, `into()` instead of
     `iter().copied().chain([..]).collect()`.
 H6  resolve (async): the unfiltered-host check and the filter move to the new private
     `allowed_addresses(&self, host: &String, resolved) -> Option<Vec<SocketAddr>>` (`None` iff
     the policy allows no address; the filter as a `for` loop pushing the allowed addresses);
     the async shell keeps `normalize_host`, the lookup, `warn!` and the error message, and
     maps `Some`/`None` to `Ok`/`Err`.
 H7  literal_ip and allows_url: parameter `url` renamed `target`.
 H8  normalize_host: `prim::trim_end_dots(host)` instead of `host.trim_end_matches('.')`.
 H9  auth.rs AuthorizationManager::is_loopback_metadata_host: `metadata_resolver::prim::
     trim_end_dots` and `metadata_resolver::prim::ends_with` instead of `trim_end_matches('.')`
     and `ends_with`.

Why each hunk is needed (measured 2026-11-25 in a scratch copy, cumulatively: each error below
is the first one Aeneas or Charon reports once the hunks before it are applied, with the Charon
settings and scripts above; the hunks were not each reverted alone):
 H1  "[Error] Dynamic trait types are not supported yet" on MetadataAddressResolver
     (metadata_resolver.rs lines 93-98) and on reqwest dns/resolve.rs line 21 (`Resolving`);
     Aeneas fails (CFailure, exit 2). Charon itself accepts the field.
 H2  The signature of with_lookup has `Arc<dyn Resolve>` (the H1 error); the match guard gives
     "[Error] Internal error" (interp/Interp.ml line 686) on lines 111-120; `Arc::new([])` gives
     "Invalid inputs for unsized cast: Arc<[String; 0]> -> Arc<[String]>".
 H3  `Arc::new(SystemResolver)` coerces to `Arc<dyn Resolve>` (the H1 error) and std::env::var
     is I/O. Not needed for the other targets: without H3, N03 is not a target (kept by human
     decision 2026-11-25).
 H4  "[Error] Internal error" on the Iterator trait (core iterator.rs line 42) from
     `Iterator::chain` (present with only with_proxy_hosts, or only allowing_private_addresses,
     as start point); "[Error] Unimplemented" on the signature of `str::contains` (the
     `core::str::pattern::Pattern` trait has a generic associated type); "Unimplemented" on
     `FnOnce for normalize_host` (a fn item used as a closure). `format!` translates (measured
     alone) but needs models of alloc::fmt::format over core::fmt::Arguments, String's
     Display::fmt and core::hint::must_use; it is replaced to keep the external models small.
 H5  The `Iterator::chain` internal error (as H4).
 H6  The async block and `Resolving` (the H1 error) cannot be translated; the
     filter/collect form translates but needs Iterator::filter (no Aeneas model: the external
     function `filter` and the external type core::iter::adapters::filter::Filter), so it is a
     loop.
 H7  Not a translation error: the Lean build fails ("Invalid field `Url`: the environment does
     not contain `url.Url.Url`"), since Aeneas emits `url.Url.host url` with a local variable
     named `url` that shadows the namespace. Remove H7 when Aeneas qualifies the name
     (`_root_.url...`). Kept without an upstream report (lead decision 2026-11-25).
 H8  "[Error] Unimplemented" on the signature of `str::trim_end_matches` (Pattern).
 H9  "[Error] Unimplemented" on `str::trim_end_matches` and `str::ends_with` (Pattern).
No upstream Charon or Aeneas issue has been filed (as of 2026-11-25); the variants are kept
outside the repository.

Why the behaviour is unchanged: every value computed is the same and in the same order. Lookup
is a newtype whose derived Clone clones the Arc (as before) and `.0.resolve` is the same call;
the nested match takes the same arm for each host; an empty `Arc<[String]>` from `Vec::new()`
equals `Arc::new([])`; `to_vec` + `push`/loop + `Arc::from(Vec)` yields the elements of the old
`chain(..).collect()` in the same order; `"http://".to_owned()` + `push_str(&proxy)` is the
string `format!("http://{proxy}")` (String's Display writes the str); the closure calls
normalize_host as the fn item did; allowed_addresses returns Some(resolved) for an unfiltered
host (also if empty), else the allowed addresses in order, or None if there is none, and the
shell maps these to exactly the old Ok/Err values, warning only on Err as before; the
environment is read in PROXY_ENV_VARS order, after with_base_url (which reads no environment)
and before the hosts are added, as the old lazy iterator did inside with_proxy_hosts; renaming a
parameter changes nothing.
Warnings: cargo clippy --lib on the patched copy (translated feature configuration, 2026-11-25)
reports two new ones, and the crate does not deny warnings: dead_code on with_lookup (in the
non-test lib build it is now used only by tests) and clippy::redundant_closure on
`|host| normalize_host(host)` in proxy_host. The closure is deliberate: with the fn item
`.map(normalize_host)` of the original (only that line reverted, every other hunk applied,
measured 2026-11-25) Aeneas reports "[Error] Unimplemented" on the signature of the compiler's
`FnOnce` impl for the fn item (`for<'_0_1> normalize_host<'_0_1>`, a higher-ranked lifetime),
cannot translate the body of proxy_host and exits 1.
Tests: cargo test --lib (features request-state, server, client, client-side-sse,
transport-streamable-http-server, transport-streamable-http-client, auth, macros) on the patched
copy: all pass, including the 16 metadata_resolver tests (counts in
formal/trusted/evidence/README.md).
